<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="060" project="dotnet-10-upgrade-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>NFR-06 — rehearse rollback (swap-back) — DEFERRED to future demo/prod stand-up on net10</title>
    <phase>P6 Production cutover (DEFERRED — OPERATOR-DRIVEN)</phase>
    <gate>deferred: demo/prod environment (re)provisioned on net10</gate>
    <status>deferred</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Production-safety rehearsal; the rollback guarantee for the cutover; deployment-critical.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Execute + verify the swap-back per runbook; well-specified, high-stakes.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>OPERATOR-DRIVEN — real slot; must precede the forward swap (061).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>051</deps>
    <tags>deployment, dotnet, migration</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>⏸ DEFERRED (owner 2026-08-11): demo/trial + production are decommissioned for budget until a first release ships, and will be re-provisioned on .NET 10 later. This task and its NFR-06 rollback-rehearsal obligation do NOT apply to the current dev-only cutover (task 051) — there is no production slot to rehearse against today. It fires ONLY when demo/prod are (re)stood-up on net10. When it does: OPERATOR-DRIVEN — rehearse the rollback (prove a swap-back returns cleanly) on the provisioned slot BEFORE the production forward swap (task 061). The procedure is documented in the task-042 slot-swap runbook (future-prod section).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE release engineer. Expert in App Service slot swaps, swap-back rollback, and zero-downtime cutover safety. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>The swap-back (net10 → 8.0) is demonstrated on the slot and returns cleanly; `notes/rollback-rehearsal.md` records the evidence, confirming the rollback path works before the production forward swap.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec NFR-06 + design §7 (rollback = swap again; staging holds the 8.0 app + runtime). The whole safety argument for the cutover (design §3/§4 principle 3) is that runtime + binary swap atomically and rollback is another swap. Proving swap-back BEFORE the forward swap is what makes the production cutover reversible.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/slot-swap-runbook.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/nonprod-smoke.md</file>
      <file role="new">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/rollback-rehearsal.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="051" status="pending">Non-prod smoke passed with a recorded "go".</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="NFR-06">Rollback MUST be rehearsed (swap-back to 8.0 proven) BEFORE the production forward swap — this task is a hard precondition for 061.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">OPERATOR-DRIVEN: real slot + credentials. Record actual swap evidence, not an assertion.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Slot swap-back rollback rehearsal</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/bff-deploy/SKILL.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="rollback-by-swap" location="projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/design.md">design §7 step 6 — rollback = swap again (staging holds 8.0).</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load spec NFR-06 + design §7 + the runbook. Declare RIGOR: FULL. Confirm operator + a recorded "go" from 051.</step>
    <step order="1">Confirm the staging slot holds a known-good 8.0 app + runtime as the rollback target.</step>
    <step order="2">Rehearse the swap-back (net10 → 8.0) on the slot; verify a clean return to 8.0 (health + a quick smoke).</step>
    <step order="3">Record the rehearsal evidence in `notes/rollback-rehearsal.md`.</step>
    <step order="4">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set 060 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="5">Document any deviation in `projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the swap-back does NOT return cleanly to 8.0, STOP and surface per CLAUDE.md §6 — the production forward swap (061) MUST NOT proceed without a proven rollback path.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">n/a (az CLI)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="doc">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/rollback-rehearsal.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The swap-back (net10 → 8.0) is demonstrated on the slot and returns cleanly (health + smoke green on 8.0).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`notes/rollback-rehearsal.md` records the actual swap evidence.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: if swap-back fails, task 061 is blocked and the failure is escalated.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec NFR-06. DEFERRED (owner 2026-08-11) — production/demo decommissioned; fires when they are re-provisioned on net10. Hard precondition for task 061 (also deferred). Procedure preserved in the task-042 runbook. See memory `active-environments`.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
